The story that describes about why Git introduced earlier

Once upon a time there were three persons from a company are invited to work on building an website called as Bharat.com
so they have to work on that website with the help of using a centralized server
If they want to upgrade any pages of the website they need to  came to the central server for the updating process

So there are lot many disadvantages on going through these process
1)The first problem was that,these persons cannot work independently
2)They cannot have code on there Laptops
3)lack of awareness on the updation of project(like one person cannot know which person changed the code,update the code and some of the time of updations of the code)

now lets discuss about version control system

These version control system helps to overcome the third disadvantage
By using these version control system ..............

1) ..............people can work Independently........................
Here that means they were allowed to work on there personal laptop and upload the updated version of their code on the website if need
And they can work on their flexible time also  which makes easy for the developer to work on specified project

2)..............Provides Better status of the Project...................
Here the developer cannot approach the co-team members for the status of the project
Because these Version control system Keep The Track or record of each and every task that anyone going to change or update or create a new different code

Example:

We are aware of the new version of the gmail and old version of the gmail also
So very rarely sometimes when the particular message was not opened due to network issue as the new version the mail was very heavy due to the vertical CSS
So it ask us to use the older version to open that message as the older version was light in weight due to less CSS and Ready to opened in low internet situations also
That means they are stored there older version of Gmail,Which takes the user to back to the older version and also allowed the user to use that in some situations

Another type of generalised example was that if we created any website based on the current needs but later if the customer was not satisfied with that website
Then what we should do we have to consider the required needs of the customers and started working on the development of the new website
But to overcome these issue we can use these version control system which allows as to update the older version of teh website with the new version
And it was also allows as to use the preferred version based on our requirement which means we can also switch to the other version from the existed version

So these kind of information about the updates and etc are stored with the help of the version control system
These version control system easily keep track of each and every thing that developer what to upgrade
We can also have the track of the entire file system and folder structure
These having information like............
 who change the code ?
 why he changed the code?
 At which part he changed the code?

 Different types of version control systems :

 Distributed Version control system..........
 1)Developer have local copy of entire project
 2)Offline work possible
 3)Changes in project can be merged later

 Centralized Version control system............
 1)Stores all project files in single central repository on a server
 2)Need developers to work on "check out" files
 3)Need developers to work on "Check in" files for updating the central repository

 GIT hub,GIT Lab, Mercurial ,Bit Bucket,Azure     - Distributed Version control system
 Apache subversion,cvs(concurrent version system) - Centralized Version control system

 Git hub    --> Online platform or cloud repository
