 Git commands.....................

 git init                         -  It means that we are going to initialize(making it ready) these entire folder as a git Repository/local Repository
 git statues                      -  It tells about the status as the number of files commited
 git add --a                      -  It was used to add all the files that we want to work on
 git commit -m "initial commit"   -  It was used to save the added files with message called as initial commit(her "-m" indicates message)
 git branch -M main               -  Here main is a folder for github repository inside which our code needs to be visible(here these command turns our master folder - main folder)
 git remote add origin github_url -  Here git - git commands | remote - To access something online | add - we can add or store the information of entire link/repository into a variable called as origin(so if next time we want to perform any operation we cannot use the entire link but we can simply use the variable name)
 git push -U origin main          -  Here push means uploading the entire information into main folder of the origin variable

 git pull                         -  These command was going to pull the changes that what we have done on the entire (It tells/shows us about the changes that are made newly)

 last three commands are used to upload the latest Information(changes in the code) into these github website and share it with others with the help of the link
 Here we have to perform these commands at once only we need not perform them again and again

 1)we have to initialize the repository
 2)we have to check the status
 3)we have to add the files to that repository
 4)we have to check the status
 5)we have to commit them(we have to save them permanently)  - Its like ctrl+s
 6)we have to check the status
 7)we have to push or upload them to that repository

 here after 5)th step we check the status for knowing about the untracked files or added files
 If the files are not saved then we need to add them with the help of command...........(git add  --a)
 Then to check that files are added or not we have to go through the command called as ..........(git status)
 so after adding the remaining files we again have to commit them(we have to save them) with the help of command.......... (git commit -m "secondary commit")
 then as a result we can see that new files are added and the current status of the repository

  sometimes we have to add a new file in one of the subfolders of the project repository
  so at that time if we use (git add --a) command and (git commit -m "initial commit" )command and check the status of the folder where new file was added
  Then we can observe that the file in that current folder was not saved so to overcome these issue we use (git add . ) which add the files to the current working directory.
  we have to enter the command(cd ..) it takes us back to the folder that previously existed
  Then we can perform commit through(git commit -m "After adding some files through folder ")
  after that we can again check our entire working of the git repository with command(git status)

  Important : SO anytime we add new lines in the files,then we have to go through the commands called as..........
  1)git add -a
  2)git commit
  3)git status
  so these three commands were not enough because the changes that we made are only changed in the vscode not in the github so to make our github also be updated we have to use these command.........
  4)git push

  Secret command : It was used to avoid the usage of (git add -a and git commit) commands
