  Note 2 : So if anyone wants to clone our repository or we want to clone others repository the command was...........
  1)git clone repository_link
  Here clone means creating copy of that entire repository

  Note 3 : If we want to add one file then the command was ......... (git add --filename)

  Note 4 : We dont have to memorize the commands but need to understand the working of that command

  overview on git commands :
  1)git init                   - Initializing the folder as git local repository
  2)git add --a                - Include files into git local repository to keep track
  3)git commit -M "message"    - Save information of files into git local repository
  4)git status                 - To check the status of any pending files
  5)git branch -m main         - Here branch is a folder where our master folder - main folder
  6)git remote add origin link - Here our link was stored in a variable called as origin so that everyone can use it remotely
  7)git push -U origin main    - Here we are pushing our information in origin into the main folder 
  8)git push                   - Rest of the time if we want to push we can use these command(to upload everytime in origin inside main)
  9)git clone https://         - To make our teammates to access our repository  
  These are the three commands(5,6,7) that we only need to perform once in the starting only


